id: 7
hanzi: 装
pinyin: zhuāng
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to load; pack; hold; install; pretend; outfit
  es: cargar; empacar; contener; instalar; fingir; vestimenta

senses[3]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to put things into a container; pack or load goods | meter o colocar objetos dentro de un recipiente o medio de transporte | 把行李装进后备箱 (pack luggage into the car trunk)
  2 | Verb | Standard | to assemble, fit, or install equipment | fijar, acoplar o montar un mecanismo o dispositivo | 在墙上装空调 (install an air conditioner on the wall)
  3 | Verb | Standard | to pretend; feign; disguise oneself | aparentar o disimular un estado o sentimiento que no es real | 装作不知情 (pretend not to know)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 出发去机场前，她把所有重要证件和笔记本电脑都仔细地装进了随身背包里。 | Chūfā qù jīchǎng qián, tā bǎ suǒyǒu zhòngyào zhèngjiàn hé bǐjìběn diànnǎo dōu zǐxì de zhuāng jìn le suíshēn bēibāo lǐ. | Before setting off for the airport, she carefully packed all her vital documents and laptop into her carry-on backpack. | Antes de salir hacia el aeropuerto, guardó minuciosamente en su mochila todos los documentos esenciales y el portátil.
  #2 | 技术工人正在实验室内给新型机器人安装高精度的激光雷达传感器。 | Jìshù gōngrén zhèng zài shíyànshì nèi gěi xīnxíng jīqìrén ānzhuāng gāo jīngdù de jīguāng léidá chuángǎnqì. | Technicians in the laboratory are currently installing high-precision LiDAR sensors onto the prototype robot. | Los técnicos montaban en el laboratorio sensores láser de alta precisión en el nuevo prototipo robótico.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  装满 | filled up with; pack full
  安装 | install; assemble
  包装 | package; wrap
  装车 | load onto a vehicle
  伪装 | disguise; camouflage
  装模作样 | put on an act; affect airs

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  装模作样 | zhuāng mú zuò yàng | put on an act; behave with affectation
  装聋作哑 | zhuāng lóng zuò yǎ | pretend to be deaf and mute; play dumb
  乔装打扮 | qiáo zhuāng dǎ bàn | disguise oneself in elaborate clothes
  满载而归 | mǎn zài ér guī | return fully loaded with riches

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  装 | zhuāng | load; pack; attire; install | cargar; vestir; montar; fingir | 衣 | clothing | 衣 (garments / outer cover) | 壮 (zhuàng / sturdy; phonetic) | 12 | 上下结构 | Sturdy 壮 on top over clothing 衣; packing oneself into robust travel attire, later expanded to packing goods and installing fixtures. | A sturdy warrior (壮) donning protective travel clothes (衣) and packing his provisions (装). | Un recio soldado (壮) vistiéndose con atuendos resistentes (衣) y cargando sus vituallas (装). | 55 | VGHO | 裝

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A sturdy warrior (壮) dressing in heavy clothing (衣) packs supplies and installs gear (装).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Un guerrero fuerte (壮) poniéndose ropa (衣) para empacar y montar su equipo de viaje (装).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Began as preparing baggage and outfitting oneself for distant expeditions along trade routes.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Level high tone: 'zhuāng' (55). Pronounce with sustained high vocal pitch without fading.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    装 | zhuāng | pack; install; pretend | Has clothing radical 衣 at bottom
    妆 | zhuāng | makeup; cosmetics | Has woman radical 女 beside 丬
    壮 | zhuàng | sturdy; strong | Upper part without the 衣 base
    袋 | dài | bag; sack | Has 代 on top over 衣
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    载 | zài | load; carry onboard
    盛 | chéng | hold in vessel; ladle
    填 | tián | fill; stuff
    配 | pèi | mate; equip; configure

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 装 covers both placing contents into a container and mounting/fixing parts onto a frame.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 装 vs. 盛 | chéng | 盛 specifically refers to ladling or holding food/liquids in open bowls (盛饭, 盛汤), while 装 applies broadly to packing luggage or freight.
    2 | 装 vs. 载 | zài | 载 focuses on transportation vehicles bearing payload weight (载重, 载客), while 装 emphasizes the manual packing action.
    3 | 装 vs. 假装 | jiǎzhuāng | 假装 exclusively denotes psychological pretense, whereas 装 has rich mechanical and physical cargo meanings.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 母亲总觉得出门在外的游子照顾不好自己。每次临别前，她都会把亲手腌制的小菜和厚实的防寒衣物，一层一层结结实实地装满整个行李箱。那沉甸甸的分量里，装载着道不尽的挂念与深情。 | Mǔqīn zǒng juéde chūmén zàiwài de yóuzǐ zhàogù bù hǎo zìjǐ. Měicì línbié qián, tā dōu huì bǎ qīnshǒu yānzhì de xiǎocài hé hòushi de fánghán yīwù, yì céng yì céng jiējiē-shíshí de zhuāngmǎn zhěnggè xínglǐxiāng. Nà chéndiāndiān de fènliàng lǐ, zhuāngzài zhe dào bú jìn de guàniàn yǔ shēnqíng. | Mother always worried her traveling child could not care for himself. Before departures, she packed homemade preserves and heavy winter coats tightly into his suitcase. Within that heavy load lay inexhaustible maternal tenderness. | La madre temía que su hijo pasara privaciones lejos de casa. Antes de cada despedida, empacaba en la maleta viandas caseras y ropa de abrigo. En aquel equipaje repleto viajaba un cariño maternal incondicional.
  #2 | 在奈史密斯发明篮球之初，工人们把两只用来装桃子的竹筐安装在阳台栏杆下方。然而每次球投进筐里后，都需要人专门踩着梯子把球取出来。为了解决这个麻烦，人们后来才锯掉筐底，实现了篮球顺畅下落的连贯比赛节奏。 | Zài Nàishǐmīsī fāmíng lánqiú zhī chū, gōngrénmen bǎ liǎng zhī yònglái zhuāng táozi de zhúkuāng ānzhuāng zài yángtái lángān xiàfāng. Rán'ér měicì qiú tóu jìn kuāng lǐ hòu, dōu xūyào rén zhuānmén cǎi zhe tīzi bǎ qiú qǔ chūlái. Wèile jiějué zhè ge máfan, rénmen hòulái cái jù diào kuāngdǐ, shíxiàn le lánqiú shùnchàng xiàluò de liánguàn bǐsài jiézòu. | At basketball's birth, workers mounted two baskets once used to hold peaches beneath the gallery railing. But after each goal, someone had to climb a ladder to extract the ball. To solve this hassle, they later sawed off the basket bottoms to let the ball drop through freely. | En los orígenes del baloncesto, se instalaron canastas de melocotones bajo la galería. Mas tras cada canasta, se requería trepar a una escalera para sacar el balón. Para agilizar el juego, se serruchó el fondo, permitiendo un flujo continuo.
